// `a[i] = v` on an array is a rebinding of the name, so it needs the name to be rebindable. The
// message is the ordinary `val` one because the statement really is an assignment by the time it is
// checked -- nothing about index assignment had to restate it.
fn main() {
    val xs = [1, 2, 3]
    xs[0] = 9
    print(xs)
}
